**Development Machine, OS, Compiler (and Other Relevant Toolchain Info)**

Ubuntu 18.04.1 LTS

**SDK Version (Please Give Commit SHA if Manually Compiling)**

1.2.12

**Protocol**

AMQP

**Describe the Bug**

When using SetOption to set OPTION_PRODUCT_INFO, the product info is not included in the Client Version when the AMQP registration happens.  The issue seems to be that the registration happens once CreateFromConnectionString is called, so when SetOption is called afterwards, the new product info isn't included.

Here are a few printf statements that illustrate the issue:
> make_product_info result: iothubclient/1.2.12 (native; Linux; x86_64)

> set result->product_info (initialize_iothub_client): iothubclient/1.2.12 (native; Linux; x86_64)

> IoTHubClientCore_LL_GetProductInfo: iothubclient/1.2.12 (native; Linux; x86_64)

> AMQP device_create

> AMQP clone_device_config

> clone_device_config: iothubclient/1.2.12 (native; Linux; x86_64)

> make_product_info result: device-agent iothubclient/1.2.12 (native; Linux; x86_64)

> set handleData->product_info (OPTION_PRODUCT_INFO): device-agent iothubclient/1.2.12 (native; Linux; x86_64)


```
IOTHUB_CLIENT_RESULT optionSetResult;
IOTHUB_DEVICE_CLIENT_LL_HANDLE clientHandle = IoTHubDeviceClient_LL_CreateFromConnectionString(connectionStringInfo.connectionString.c_str(), AMQP_Protocol);
optionSetResult = IoTHubDeviceClient_LL_SetOption(_deviceClientHandle, OPTION_PRODUCT_INFO, IoTHubClientProductInfo);
```

