In this thread I couldn's see an issue with the code till I actually tested and realised that there must be something wrong with the rate limit of `Particle.publish()`.
Although we are allowed one publish per second, going close - but not over - that limit causes frequent cloud disconnect/reconnect glitches.

With this code on a Photon running 0.5.1 I get consistent reconnects every 60sec.

``` cpp
const uint32_t msPublish = 1000;

void setup() {
}

void loop() {
    static uint32_t ms;

    if (millis() - ms > msPublish)
    {
        ms = millis();
        Particle.publish("ScruffyTest", "Dummy!", PRIVATE);
    }
}
```

But when I increase `msPublish = 1100` the problem goes away - but even `1005` is too little (`1010` seems to be OK in most cases)

