### Expected behavior

When using Particle.publish( ... , WITH_ACK); if the message cannot be sent due to internet loss, the function call should timeout after 30 seconds.  Docs do not state the timeout expected either.

### Observed behavior

The function call blocks until the internet returns, or the Wi-Fi AP is turned off completely.

### Steps to reproduce

WITH_ACK only available using 0.6.1 firmware. Run the test app below, and either pull the ethernet cable between the modem and router, or switch off the internet connection in your router settings if available.

### Test App

```c
SYSTEM_MODE(SEMI_AUTOMATIC);
SYSTEM_THREAD(ENABLED);

const uint32_t PUBLISH_INVERVAL = 2000;
int count = 1;

void setup() {
    Particle.connect();
    Serial.begin();
}

void loop() {
    static uint32_t lastPublish;

    if (millis() - lastPublish > PUBLISH_INVERVAL)
    {
        lastPublish = millis();
        bool success = false;
        success = Particle.publish("publish-with-ack", String(count), PRIVATE, WITH_ACK);
        if (!success) {
            Serial.printlnf("%7d(s): publish failed: %d", millis()/1000, count);
        }
        else {
            Serial.printlnf("%7d(s): publish passed: %d", millis()/1000, count);
        }
        count++;
    }
}
```

